# /etc/trend-investing/secrets.env  (root:root, mode 0600, outside the repository)
# Names only; the owner fills the values on the server. Passed to the data step
# (ti-data.service), the engines (ti-engine@.service), the reporter
# (ti-reporter@.service) and the Flex reader (ti-flex@.service) through
# systemd LoadCredential and read by them from
# $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY/secrets. The dashboard is given none. Never put the
# IBKR login here.
# IBKR account numbers: names kept for the IRA engines; no program reads them yet. The Boost account's
# number is not here: it is in /etc/trend-investing/accounts/boost.env
# (deploy/etc/accounts/boost.env.example), the only file its adapter is given.
IBKR_ACCOUNT_TRAD_IRA=
IBKR_ACCOUNT_ROTH_IRA=
# Massive market-data key, for the data step (ti-data reads only this line;
# plan.md section 4). The owner's own key from massive.com; never committed,
# never printed.
MASSIVE_API_KEY=
# Alerting (plan.md section 7), read by the reporter (ti-reporter@<instance>)
# for its two channels; docs/manual/alerts-and-dashboard.md, "Where alerts go".
# TI_NTFY_TOPIC: an unguessable ntfy topic name; it is the ntfy secret.
# TI_NTFY_SERVER: your own ntfy server's URL, http://<this server's Tailscale
# address>:2586, which `provision.sh ntfy` prints. Empty means the public
# https://ntfy.sh relay. The daily summary carries balances, so it goes only
# to your own server: never to the public relay or to PagerDuty, and without
# your own server it is not sent.
# TI_PAGERDUTY_ROUTING_KEY: the PagerDuty Events API v2 integration key.
# The reporter refuses to run, and its unit fails, while either required
# value is empty. The outside dead-man's switch (a heartbeat to a service off
# this server) is not built, so there is no line for it.
TI_NTFY_TOPIC=
TI_NTFY_SERVER=
TI_PAGERDUTY_ROUTING_KEY=
# IBKR Flex Web Service, read by each account's Flex reader
# (ti-flex@<instance>.service) for the account's deposits and withdrawals;
# docs/manual/reconciliation.md, "Deposits and withdrawals, read from IBKR".
# TI_IBKR_FLEX_TOKEN: the Flex Web Service token the owner generates in
# Client Portal; it is the Flex secret, sent to IBKR only.
# TI_IBKR_FLEX_QUERY_ID: the ID of the owner's saved Flex query holding the
# Cash Transactions section. The reader refuses to run while either is empty.
TI_IBKR_FLEX_TOKEN=
TI_IBKR_FLEX_QUERY_ID=
